          "login": "KageBinary",
          "id": 107007243,
          "type": "User",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/KageBinary"
        },
        "body": "Reviewed. The renamed-import fix is correct and the cross-batch path holds up — `filePublicNames`/`fileHasSymbol` are single merged maps, so same-batch and cross-batch are the same branch.\n\nOne defect to fix before merge: the new fallback matches `binding.imported` against every parsed symbol, and for a default import that value is the literal sentinel `'default'`, not an export name. Any provider member *called* `default` — a method, getter, or static — then satisfies it and produces a 0.9-confidence edge to the wrong member. Existing tests all use a named default export (`export default actualName`), which resolves earlier, which is why CI is green.\n\nFix + regression test (mutation-tested): **Hiro-Chiba/Ix#1** → merge it into `fix/renamed-type-imports` and this PR updates in place.",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/ix-infrastructure/Ix/pull/434#issuecomment-5295706429",
        "api_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ix-infrastructure/Ix/issues/comments/5295706429",
